From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Blumenkrantz <michael.blumenkrantz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:47:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: don't let the queue submit thread inherit a pinned
 affinity

the submit thread is created from the app thread, which mesa_pin_threads
may have pinned to one cpu

Generated-by: LLM
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45386>
(cherry picked from commit afe1e0d5026d3879af483357ff21ae99be4ecba0)
---
 src/vulkan/runtime/vk_queue.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_queue.c b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_queue.c
index 78439dbbefb..52cd5527f92 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_queue.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_queue.c
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 
 #include "util/perf/cpu_trace.h"
 #include "util/u_debug.h"
+#include "util/u_thread.h"
 #include <inttypes.h>
 
 #include "vk_alloc.h"
@@ -738,6 +739,8 @@ vk_queue_submit_thread_func(void *_data)
    struct vk_queue *queue = _data;
    VkResult result;
 
+   util_set_current_thread_full_affinity();
+
    mtx_lock(&queue->submit.mutex);
 
    while (queue->submit.thread_run) {
-- 
2.53.0

